## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical diagnostic reasoning for common cross-region latency issues, focusing on DNS routing, TLS termination, and edge pathing rather than code changes.

## Key Concepts

- DNS routing and TTL effects
- TLS handshake timing across regions
- Edge NAT/firewall behavior and LB logs
- Basic network measurement tools (dig, curl, mtr, openssl)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: measure DNS and HTTP timings in Node.js
const https = require('https');
const start = Date.now();
https.get('https://api.example.com/ping', res => {
  res.resume();
  res.on('end', () => console.log('elapsed', Date.now() - start));
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- What are trade-offs between low vs high DNS TTL in this setup, and how would you monitor them?
- How would you validate TLS termination consistency across regions without changing apps?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical DNS- and LB-related troubleshooting that intermediate engineers confront in global deployments. It emphasizes data collection, reproducibility, and concrete mitigations rather than theory.

## Key Concepts
- DNS TTL and resolver caching
- Geolocation-based routing rules
- Regional load balancer health checks and failover
- Traceroute/tracepath, dig +trace, and MTR for path visibility

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple DNS lookup example using Node.js
const dns = require('dns');
dns.resolve4('api.example.com', (err, addresses) => {
  console.log(addresses, err);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design a minimal reproducible test for this issue?
- What mitigations would you apply if you must avoid application changes?
